Input: {"decision_time_ms": 1790279999999, "macro_contexts": {"D1": {"context": {"always_in": "long", "always_in_relevance": "medium", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790207999999, "directional_pressure": "bull", "evidence_against": ["The leg since bar 84 spends about 25 bars (87-111) inside a two-sided 2357.18-2680 band, so the leg is at least as range-like as trend-like and could be classified trading-range/channel rather than bull-trend.", "Momentum faded at the highs: bar 86 spiked to 2771 but closed 2515.3 with a long upper tail, and the 2643-2850 top area shows overlapping bars rather than clean trend bars.", "Bar 119 closes near its low (2684.16 in a 2641.37-2786.81 range) after a marginal new high 2850 versus the 2771 spike high, so an MTR from the high is not excluded.", "The first 84 bars of the window are bearish then rangebound, so the bull case rests only on roughly the last 36 bars."], "evidence_for": ["Higher swing lows dominate after bar 84: 2111 (bar 85 low), 2325.31 (bar 86 low), 2357.18 (bar 99 low), 2358.62 (bar 111 low), 2435.72 (bar 107 low).", "Higher swing highs over the same span: 2348.02 (bar 85), 2771 (bar 86), 2680 (bar 107), 2850 (bar 117).", "Bull bodies carry the advance: bar 84 opens 1916.51 and closes 2252.16, bar 107 opens 2437 and prints 2680, and bars 113-117 run from 2446.22 to a 2775.61 close.", "The current two-bar set-back (bars 118-119) is no deeper than the repeated pullbacks inside the 87-111 band, which is normal pullback behavior inside a bull leg."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["Bars 0-10 form a bear leg: close slides from 2072.8 to 1568.55 and the window low 1368.42 is set on bar 10 (low 1368.42, close 1568.55).", "Bars 11-83 are a broad two-sided base bounded by low 1512.91 (bar 30) and high 1974.46 (bar 61); bars overlap heavily and every multi-bar swing is retraced.", "Bar 84 is a large bull breakout bar out of that base: open 1916.51, high 2293.8, low 1905.63, close 2252.16.", "Bar 85 closes 2326.32 (high 2348.02, low 2111); bar 86 spikes to 2771 but closes 2515.3, leaving a long upper tail.", "Bars 87-111 overlap in a 2357.18 (bar 99 low) to 2680 (bar 107 high) band, then bars 112-117 rally from 2358.62 to a new high 2850 (bar 117, close 2775.61).", "Bars 118-119 are consecutive bear bars; bar 119 opens 2752.43, trades 2641.37-2786.81 and closes 2684.16, in the lower part of its range and below bar 118's 2752.43 close."], "phase": "channel", "primary_regime": "bull-trend", "role": "CONTEXT_ANALYST", "schema": "brooks.market-context.v2", "structures": [{"description": "Two-sided base after the opening bear leg: about 73 bars oscillating with heavy overlap between the 1512.91 low (bar 30) and the 1974.46 high (bar 61), with repeated failed pushes in both directions.", "end_time_ms": 1787097599999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "1512.91", "start_time_ms": 1780790400000, "upper_boundary": "1974.46"}, {"description": "Bull spike out of the base: bar 84 (open 1916.51, high 2293.8, close 2252.16) clears the base by a wide margin, bar 85 closes 2326.32, bar 86 spikes to 2771 and closes 2515.3. No exact horizontal boundary is claimed for this impulsive leg.", "end_time_ms": 1787356799999, "kind": "breakout", "lower_boundary": null, "start_time_ms": 1787097600000, "upper_boundary": null}, {"description": "Post-spike consolidation and channel-like portion of the bull leg: bars 87-111 overlap between low 2357.18 (bar 99) and high 2680 (bar 107) while keeping higher lows, so the leg is channel-like rather than a clean spike.", "end_time_ms": 1789516799999, "kind": "range", "lower_boundary": "2357.18", "start_time_ms": 1787356800000, "upper_boundary": "2680"}, {"description": "Two-bar bear reversal attempt at the bull high: bar 117 makes a new high 2850 and closes 2775.61, then bars 118-119 turn down and bar 119 closes 2684.16 near its low. Higher high over the 2771 spike high (bar 86) plus only two bear bars means this is a potential reversal pattern, not a confirmed reversal.", "end_time_ms": 1790207999999, "kind": "mtr-like", "lower_boundary": "2641.37", "start_time_ms": 1789948800000, "upper_boundary": "2850"}], "symbol": "ETH-USDT", "timeframe": "D1", "transition_conditions": ["Bull continuation is supported if a bar closes above 2786.81 (bar 119 high) and then above 2850 (bar 117 high) with a strong bull body and little overlap.", "A close below 2641.37 (bar 119 low), then below 2435.72 (bar 107 low) and 2358.62 (bar 111 low), would break the sequence of higher lows and weaken the bull read.", "A close below 2325.31 (bar 86 low) would negate the post-base breakout structure and favor a major-trend-reversal or trading-range classification.", "If subsequent bars keep overlapping and closing mid-range around 2600-2800 for many sessions, the read shifts from bull-trend/channel toward trading-range/range."], "window_bars": 120}, "freshness": "current"}, "H4": {"context": {"always_in": "unclear", "always_in_relevance": "low", "breakout_mode": false, "confidence": "medium", "decision_time_ms": 1790265599999, "directional_pressure": "balanced", "evidence_against": ["The window's largest structure is the bull leg 2358.62 to 2850 (bars 1789488000000-1789977600000, +20.8%) with a clean higher low at 2568.16; the drop to 2633.31 is only a 44.1% retrace, which fits a bull pullback rather than a range regime.", "The 16-bar tight range 2716.01-2804.59 following the bar 1789977600000 spike has the shape of a tight flag after a strong buy spike; read that way the window is bull-trend/channel, not trading-range.", "The last 7 bars make successively lower highs (2698.06 then 2694.37) and lower lows (2648.49 then 2633.31), which supports a small bear channel from 2850 instead of a two-sided range.", "The current close 2682.25 is still below the broken 2716.01 floor, so the two-sided claim rests mainly on one reversal bar at 2633.31-2682.25."], "evidence_for": ["The last 19 bars (1789992000000-1790251199999) stay inside 2633.31-2804.59, roughly 6.5% of price, with overlapping bodies and no pair of consecutive closes beyond either extreme.", "Although bar 1790164800000 broke the 2716.01 floor, the following bars closed 2676.47, 2684.16, 2675.48 and 2692.23, none below 2659, so the downside break was not accepted.", "Bar 1790236800000's marginal new low 2633.31 was immediately reversed by bar 1790251200000 closing 2682.25 near its high, a failed downside break that leaves the range intact.", "Lower highs (2804.59, 2786.81, 2698.06, 2694.37) and lower lows (2716.01, 2648.49, 2633.31) mean neither side has held a one-sided close sequence for the ~19 bars since the 2850 spike."], "missing_information": [], "observations": ["120 closed H4 bars, 1788537600000 to 1790251199999; window envelope 2358.62 (bar 1789488000000 low) to 2850 (bar 1789977600000 high).", "Bars 1788537600000-1789113600000 overlapped inside 2411.04-2528.8; bar 1788739200000 tested 2528.8 and closed 2496.01 at its low, bar 1789041600000 tested 2411.04 and closed 2440.2.", "Bar 1789128000000 opened 2457.12, spiked to 2680 and closed 2555.52 (235.81 range, 124.48 upper tail); no later close exceeded 2609.02.", "Bar 1789416000000 rejected 2609.02 and closed 2514.07 near its low; bars 1789473600000 and 1789488000000 closed 2423.29 and 2412.95, printing the window low 2358.62.", "From 2358.62 closes rose to 2850 at bar 1789977600000 (open 2658.81, close 2723.15, 126.85 upper tail); the intervening pullback held 2568.16 at bar 1789891200000.", "Bars 1789992000000-1790150400000 overlapped in 2716.01-2804.59; bar 1790164800000 broke that floor to low 2648.49 / close 2659, and bars 1790179200000-1790236799999 stayed between 2641.37 and 2698.06 without reclaiming 2716.01.", "Bar 1790236800000 printed a marginal lower low 2633.31 and closed 2647.9, then bar 1790251200000 closed 2682.25, 77.7% of its 2640-2694.37 range, back above the 2648.49 break level."], "phase": "range", "primary_regime": "trading-range", "role": 